{"batch":1,"level":"Pre-A1","variant":"fr-FR","pedagogy":{"learner_language":"fa-IR","standard":"contemporary standard French","principles":["teach high-frequency communicative chunks before grammatical analysis","make French sound-spelling opacity explicit for Persian learners","train /u/ versus /y/ and beginner nasal vowels through listening","introduce noun gender together with articles rather than isolated labels","keep tu/vous register choices explicit and pragmatically natural","preserve accents, cedilla and apostrophes in all learner-facing French text","keep every dialogue short, coherent, culturally natural and beginner-safe"]},"units":[{"slug":"first-greetings","topic":"greetings","title":"Bonjour !","vocab":[["bonjour","bonjour","سلام / روز بخیر","expression",1],["salut","salut","سلام / خداحافظِ خودمانی","expression",1],["bonsoir","bonsoir","عصر بخیر / شب بخیر هنگام سلام","expression",1],["au_revoir","au revoir","خداحافظ","expression",2],["a_bientot","à bientôt","به‌زودی می‌بینمتان","expression",2],["enchante","enchanté / enchantée","خوشوقتم","expression",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Bonjour !","سلام!","greet_neutral",["bonjour"],1],["u2","Salut !","سلام!","greet_informal",["salut"],1],["u3","Enchanté !","خوشوقتم!","pleased_to_meet",["enchante"],2],["u4","Au revoir, à bientôt.","خداحافظ، به‌زودی می‌بینمتان.","farewell",["au_revoir","a_bientot"],2]],"grammar":["Bonjour / salut","French greetings depend on register and time of day. Bonjour is a safe neutral daytime greeting; salut is informal.","«Bonjour» برای شروع خنثی و امن در روز مناسب است؛ «salut» خودمانی است. در فرانسوی انتخاب سلام به رابطه و موقعیت بستگی دارد.",[["Bonjour, madame.","روز بخیر خانم."],["Salut, Hugo !","سلام هوگو!"]]],"dialogues":[["Premier bonjour","سلام اول",[["Camille","Bonjour !","سلام!"],["Thomas","Bonjour !","سلام!"],["Camille","Enchanté.","خوشوقتم."],["Thomas","Enchanté.","من هم خوشوقتم."]],1],["On se dit au revoir","خداحافظی",[["Léa","Salut !","خداحافظ!"],["Hugo","Salut !","خداحافظ!"],["Léa","À bientôt !","به‌زودی می‌بینمت!"],["Hugo","Oui, à bientôt.","بله، به‌زودی می‌بینمت."]],2]]},{"slug":"my-name","topic":"introductions","title":"Je m'appelle…","vocab":[["je_m_appelle","je m'appelle","اسمم ... است","expression",1],["comment","comment","چطور / چگونه","adverb",1],["tu_t_appelles","tu t'appelles","اسمت ... است","expression",1],["je_suis","je suis","من هستم","expression",2],["nom","nom","اسم / نام","noun",2],["moi","moi","من / خودم","pronoun",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Je m'appelle Camille.","اسمم کامی است.","introduce_name",["je_m_appelle"],1],["u2","Comment tu t'appelles ?","اسمت چیه؟","ask_name_informal",["comment","tu_t_appelles"],1],["u3","Je suis Thomas.","من توما هستم.","introduce_self",["je_suis"],2],["u4","Et toi ?","و تو؟","return_question",["moi"],2]],"grammar":["Je m'appelle… / Je suis…","Use Je m'appelle… as the most common beginner introduction. Je suis + first name is possible but less canonical for introducing yourself.","برای معرفی، «Je m'appelle…» الگوی اصلی و طبیعی‌تر است. «Je suis + نام» هم ممکن است، اما فعلاً معرفی با «Je m'appelle…» را پایه بگیر.",[["Je m'appelle Léa.","اسمم لئاست."],["Comment tu t'appelles ?","اسمت چیه؟"]]],"dialogues":[["Faire connaissance","آشنا شدن",[["Inès","Salut ! Je m'appelle Inès.","سلام! اسمم اینس است."],["Nicolas","Salut ! Moi, c'est Nicolas.","سلام! من نیکولا هستم."],["Inès","Enchantée.","خوشوقتم."],["Nicolas","Enchanté.","من هم خوشوقتم."]],1],["Un prénom","یک اسم",[["Claire","Bonjour, je m'appelle Claire.","سلام، اسمم کلر است."],["Julien","Bonjour, je suis Julien.","سلام، من ژولین هستم."],["Claire","Et toi ?","و تو؟"],["Julien","Moi, c'est Julien.","من ژولین هستم."]],2]]},{"slug":"numbers-0-10","topic":"numbers","title":"De zéro à dix","vocab":[["zero","zéro","صفر","number",1],["un","un","یک","number",1],["deux","deux","دو","number",1],["trois","trois","سه","number",2],["cinq","cinq","پنج","number",2],["dix","dix","ده","number",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Zéro, un, deux.","صفر، یک، دو.","count",["zero","un","deux"],1],["u2","Le numéro deux.","شماره دو.","identify_number",["deux"],1],["u3","Cinq minutes.","پنج دقیقه.","say_duration",["cinq"],2],["u4","Dix euros.","ده یورو.","say_price_amount",["dix"],2]],"grammar":["Les nombres 0–10","Learn the stable counting forms first. Final consonants are often not pronounced, so audio recognition matters from the beginning.","عددها را از همان اول با صدا یاد بگیر؛ در فرانسوی خیلی از صامت‌های پایانی نوشته می‌شوند اما همیشه تلفظ نمی‌شوند.",[["deux cafés","دو قهوه"],["cinq minutes","پنج دقیقه"]]],"dialogues":[["Quel numéro ?","کدام شماره؟",[["Camille","C'est le deux ?","شماره دو است؟"],["Hugo","Oui, le deux.","بله، دو."],["Camille","Et le trois ?","و سه؟"],["Hugo","Ici.","اینجاست."]],1],["Cinq ou dix ?","پنج یا ده؟",[["Léa","Cinq minutes ?","پنج دقیقه؟"],["Nicolas","Non, dix minutes.","نه، ده دقیقه."],["Léa","Dix ?","ده؟"],["Nicolas","Oui, dix.","بله، ده."]],2]]},{"slug":"alphabet-accents","topic":"script-basics","title":"L'alphabet et les accents","vocab":[["a_letter","A","حرف A","letter",1],["e_letter","E","حرف E","letter",1],["e_accent","é","حرف é با آکسان تِگو","letter",1],["c_cedille","ç","حرف ç با سدی","letter",2],["apostrophe","l'apostrophe","آپاستروف","noun",2],["alphabet","alphabet","الفبا","noun",2]],"utterances":[["u1","C'est la lettre A.","این حرف A است.","identify_letter",["a_letter"],1],["u2","É a un accent.","É یک آکسان دارد.","notice_accent",["e_accent"],1],["u3","Garçon contient ç.","کلمهٔ «garçon» حرف ç دارد.","notice_cedilla",["c_cedille"],2],["u4","Je vois une apostrophe.","یک آپاستروف می‌بینم.","notice_apostrophe",["apostrophe"],2]],"grammar":["Accents et apostrophe","French spelling uses accents and apostrophes as meaningful written features. Preserve them rather than treating them as decoration.","آکسان‌ها و آپاستروف در نوشتار فرانسوی تزئینی نیستند؛ شکل درست کلمه را از ابتدا با آن‌ها حفظ کن.",[["café","کافه / قهوه"],["l'école","مدرسه"]]],"dialogues":[["Une lettre","یک حرف",[["Inès","C'est A ?","این A است؟"],["Julien","Oui, c'est A.","بله، A است."],["Inès","Et ça ?","و این؟"],["Julien","C'est É.","É است."]],1],["Un accent","یک آکسان",[["Claire","Il y a un accent ?","آکسان دارد؟"],["Thomas","Oui, sur le é.","بله، روی é."],["Claire","Et l'apostrophe ?","و آپاستروف؟"],["Thomas","Elle est ici.","اینجاست."]],2]]},{"slug":"first-sounds","topic":"sound-letter-mapping","title":"Mes premiers sons","vocab":[["ou_sound","ou","صدای «او» مثل vous","grapheme",1],["u_sound","u","صدای فرانسوی u","grapheme",1],["on_sound","on","صدای خیشومی on","grapheme",1],["an_sound","an","صدای خیشومی an","grapheme",2],["ch_sound","ch","صدای ش","grapheme",2],["r_sound","r","صدای r فرانسوی","grapheme",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Vous : ou.","در «vous» صدای ou را می‌شنوی.","sound_mapping",["ou_sound"],1],["u2","Tu : u.","در «tu» صدای u را می‌شنوی.","sound_mapping",["u_sound"],1],["u3","Bonjour contient un son nasal.","«bonjour» یک صدای خیشومی دارد.","notice_nasal",["on_sound"],2],["u4","Chat commence par ch.","«chat» با ch شروع می‌شود.","sound_mapping",["ch_sound"],2]],"grammar":["Sons français essentiels","French has contrasts unfamiliar to many Persian learners, especially /u/ versus /y/ and nasal vowels. Train them through listening before detailed phonetic labels.","برای فارسی‌زبان تفاوت «ou» و «u» و همین‌طور واکه‌های خیشومی مهم است. اول با گوش و نمونه‌های کوتاه فرقشان را بگیر.",[["vous / tu","vous / tu"],["bon / banc","دو نمونه با صدای خیشومی متفاوت"]]],"dialogues":[["Ou ou u ?","ou یا u؟",[["Camille","Tu entends «ou» ?","صدای «ou» می‌شنوی؟"],["Nicolas","Oui, dans «vous».","بله، در «vous»."],["Camille","Et dans «tu» ?","و در «tu»؟"],["Nicolas","C'est «u».","آن «u» است."]],1],["Un son nasal","یک صدای خیشومی",[["Léa","Écoute : bon.","گوش کن: bon."],["Julien","J'entends «on».","صدای «on» می‌شنوم."],["Léa","Encore ?","دوباره؟"],["Julien","Bon.","bon."]],2]]},{"slug":"how-are-you","topic":"greetings","title":"Ça va ?","vocab":[["ca_va","ça va","خوبی؟ / خوبم / اوضاع چطور است","expression",1],["bien","bien","خوب","adverb",1],["tres_bien","très bien","خیلی خوب","expression",1],["mal","mal","بد","adverb",2],["merci","merci","ممنون","expression",2],["et_toi","et toi","و تو؟","expression",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Ça va ?","خوبی؟","ask_wellbeing",["ca_va"],1],["u2","Ça va bien.","خوبم.","answer_wellbeing",["ca_va","bien"],1],["u3","Très bien, merci.","خیلی خوبم، ممنون.","answer_positive",["tres_bien","merci"],2],["u4","Et toi ?","و تو؟","return_question",["et_toi"],2]],"grammar":["Ça va ?","Ça va? is a high-frequency informal wellbeing formula. The same chunk can function as question and answer depending on intonation and context.","«Ça va ?» یکی از پرکاربردترین الگوهای احوال‌پرسی است و بسته به آهنگ جمله می‌تواند سؤال یا بخشی از جواب باشد.",[["Ça va ? — Ça va.","خوبی؟ — خوبم."],["Très bien, merci.","خیلی خوبم، ممنون."]]],"dialogues":[["Ça va aujourd'hui ?","امروز خوبی؟",[["Inès","Salut ! Ça va ?","سلام! خوبی؟"],["Thomas","Oui, ça va bien.","بله، خوبم."],["Inès","Super.","عالیه."],["Thomas","Et toi ?","و تو؟"]],1],["Très bien","خیلی خوب",[["Claire","Bonjour ! Ça va ?","سلام! خوبی؟"],["Hugo","Très bien, merci.","خیلی خوبم، ممنون."],["Claire","Et toi ?","و تو؟"],["Hugo","Ça va.","خوبم."]],2]]},{"slug":"first-objects","topic":"objects","title":"Qu'est-ce que c'est ?","vocab":[["un_livre","un livre","یک کتاب","noun",1],["une_table","une table","یک میز","noun",1],["un_telephone","un téléphone","یک تلفن","noun",1],["une_cle","une clé","یک کلید","noun",2],["c_est","c'est","این / آن ... است","expression",2],["qu_est_ce","qu'est-ce que c'est","این چیست؟","expression",2]],"utterances":[["u1","C'est un livre.","این یک کتاب است.","identify_object",["c_est","un_livre"],1],["u2","C'est une table.","این یک میز است.","identify_object",["c_est","une_table"],1],["u3","Qu'est-ce que c'est ?","این چیه؟","ask_object",["qu_est_ce"],2],["u4","C'est une clé.","این یک کلید است.","identify_object",["c_est","une_cle"],2]],"grammar":["Un / une","French nouns have grammatical gender. At this stage, learn each noun together with its article: un livre, une table.","جنس دستوری را از همان اول همراه اسم یاد بگیر: به‌جای حفظ «livre»، ترکیب «un livre» را حفظ کن و برای اسم مؤنث «une table».",[["un téléphone","یک تلفن"],["une clé","یک کلید"]]],"dialogues":[["Sur la table","روی میز",[["Camille","Qu'est-ce que c'est ?","این چیه؟"],["Julien","C'est un livre.","یک کتاب است."],["Camille","Et ça ?","و این؟"],["Julien","Une clé.","یک کلید."]],1],["Un ou une ?","un یا une؟",[["Léa","Un téléphone ?","یک تلفن؟"],["Thomas","Oui, un téléphone.","بله، یک تلفن."],["Léa","Une table ?","یک میز؟"],["Thomas","Oui, une table.","بله، یک میز."]],2]]},{"slug":"polite-words","topic":"polite-language","title":"S'il vous plaît","vocab":[["s_il_vous_plait","s'il vous plaît","لطفاً (محترمانه / جمع)","expression",1],["s_il_te_plait","s'il te plaît","لطفاً (خودمانی)","expression",1],["merci","merci","ممنون","expression",1],["de_rien","de rien","خواهش می‌کنم","expression",2],["pardon","pardon","ببخشید","expression",2],["excusez_moi","excusez-moi","ببخشید (محترمانه)","expression",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Un café, s'il vous plaît.","یک قهوه لطفاً.","polite_request",["s_il_vous_plait"],1],["u2","Merci beaucoup.","خیلی ممنون.","thank",["merci"],1],["u3","De rien.","خواهش می‌کنم.","respond_thanks",["de_rien"],2],["u4","Excusez-moi.","ببخشید.","get_attention_polite",["excusez_moi"],2]],"grammar":["Tu / vous dans la politesse","French distinguishes informal tu and neutral/polite or plural vous. Learn fixed polite chunks before full pronoun grammar.","در فرانسوی «tu» خودمانی و «vous» محترمانه یا جمع است. فعلاً عبارت‌های ثابت مثل «s'il vous plaît» و «excusez-moi» را به‌صورت کامل یاد بگیر.",[["S'il vous plaît.","لطفاً."],["Merci. — De rien.","ممنون. — خواهش می‌کنم."]]],"dialogues":[["Au café","در کافه",[["Inès","Un café, s'il vous plaît.","یک قهوه لطفاً."],["Hugo","Bien sûr.","حتماً."],["Inès","Merci.","ممنون."],["Hugo","De rien.","خواهش می‌کنم."]],1],["Excusez-moi","ببخشید",[["Claire","Excusez-moi.","ببخشید."],["Nicolas","Oui ?","بله؟"],["Claire","Pardon.","معذرت می‌خواهم."],["Nicolas","Pas de problème.","مشکلی نیست."]],2]]},{"slug":"survival-words","topic":"requests","title":"Je ne comprends pas","vocab":[["oui","oui","بله","particle",1],["non","non","نه","particle",1],["je_comprends","je comprends","می‌فهمم","expression",1],["je_ne_comprends_pas","je ne comprends pas","نمی‌فهمم","expression",2],["repetez","répétez","تکرار کنید","verb",2],["lentement","lentement","آهسته","adverb",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Oui.","بله.","confirm",["oui"],1],["u2","Non.","نه.","deny",["non"],1],["u3","Je ne comprends pas.","نمی‌فهمم.","signal_noncomprehension",["je_ne_comprends_pas"],2],["u4","Répétez lentement, s'il vous plaît.","لطفاً آهسته تکرار کنید.","request_repetition",["repetez","lentement"],2]],"grammar":["Ne… pas","The standard beginner negation is ne + verb + pas. In casual speech ne is often dropped, but the course introduces the full standard form first.","الگوی استاندارد منفی «ne + فعل + pas» است. در گفتار روزمره گاهی «ne» حذف می‌شود، اما برای شروع شکل کامل و استاندارد را یاد بگیر.",[["Je comprends.","می‌فهمم."],["Je ne comprends pas.","نمی‌فهمم."]]],"dialogues":[["Je ne comprends pas","نمی‌فهمم",[["Camille","Vous comprenez ?","متوجه می‌شوید؟"],["Claire","Non, je ne comprends pas.","نه، نمی‌فهمم."],["Camille","Je répète.","تکرار می‌کنم."],["Claire","Merci.","ممنون."]],1],["Plus lentement","آهسته‌تر",[["Thomas","C'est bon ?","خوبه؟"],["Hugo","Pardon ?","ببخشید؟"],["Thomas","Je répète lentement.","آهسته تکرار می‌کنم."],["Hugo","Merci beaucoup.","خیلی ممنون."]],2]]},{"slug":"first-conversation","topic":"introductions","title":"Ma première conversation","vocab":[["bonjour","bonjour","سلام / روز بخیر","expression",1],["je_m_appelle","je m'appelle","اسمم ... است","expression",1],["ca_va","ça va","خوبی؟ / خوبم","expression",1],["merci","merci","ممنون","expression",2],["au_revoir","au revoir","خداحافظ","expression",2],["a_bientot","à bientôt","به‌زودی می‌بینمت","expression",2]],"utterances":[["u1","Bonjour, je m'appelle Claire.","سلام، اسمم کلر است.","greet_and_introduce",["bonjour","je_m_appelle"],1],["u2","Ça va ?","خوبی؟","ask_wellbeing",["ca_va"],1],["u3","Ça va bien, merci.","خوبم، ممنون.","answer_wellbeing",["ca_va","merci"],2],["u4","Au revoir, à bientôt.","خداحافظ، به‌زودی می‌بینمت.","farewell",["au_revoir","a_bientot"],2]],"grammar":["Assembler les expressions","Combine familiar chunks into a short real exchange. The aim is fluent retrieval, not new grammar.","در این واحد قرار نیست دستور تازه‌ای اضافه شود؛ هدف این است که تکه‌های آشنا را بدون مکث زیاد در یک گفت‌وگوی کوتاه کنار هم بگذاری.",[["Bonjour, je m'appelle Claire.","سلام، اسمم کلر است."],["Au revoir, à bientôt.","خداحافظ، به‌زودی می‌بینمت."]]],"dialogues":[["Première rencontre","اولین آشنایی",[["Léa","Bonjour ! Je m'appelle Léa.","سلام! اسمم لئاست."],["Inès","Bonjour ! Moi, c'est Inès.","سلام! من اینس هستم."],["Léa","Ça va ?","خوبی؟"],["Inès","Très bien, merci.","خیلی خوبم، ممنون."]],1],["À bientôt","به‌زودی می‌بینمت",[["Nicolas","Je ne comprends pas.","نمی‌فهمم."],["Julien","Je répète lentement.","آهسته تکرار می‌کنم."],["Nicolas","Merci. Au revoir !","ممنون. خداحافظ!"],["Julien","Au revoir, à bientôt !","خداحافظ، به‌زودی می‌بینمت!"]],2]]}]}